      "side": 1,
      "message": "Alright, new comments. In deference to Steven, and while striking a balance with safety, I proposed the following guideline: \"If an unsigned field will not overflow and result in a negative number in Java, go ahead and shrink its size; if the field can overflow, please use the next larger data type to ensure that signed/unsigned is not a problem.\"\n\nThere\u0027s no issue with packing fields that require bitwise interpretation since they can\u0027t be range checked as-is anyway.",
